#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Introduction {#introduction}"
msgstr "Pengenalan {#introduction}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the following video, Olivia Lanes steps you through the content in this "
"lesson. Alternatively, you can open the [YouTube "
"video](https://youtu.be/kniiVC538nY?si=13OJnaO5jyAUmoPQ) for this lesson in "
"a separate window.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam video berikut, Olivia Lanes membimbing Anda melalui kandungan dalam "
"pelajaran ini. Sebagai alternatif, Anda boleh buka [video "
"YouTube](https://youtu.be/kniiVC538nY?si=13OJnaO5jyAUmoPQ) untuk pelajaran "
"ini dalam tetingkap berasingan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<IBMVideo id=\"134786191\" title=\"In this video Olivia walks you through "
"finding the energy of a two-qubit Ising Hamiltonian using the Estimator "
"primitive in Qiskit.\"/>\n"
msgstr ""
"<IBMVideo id=\"134786191\" title=\"Dalam video ini Olivia membimbing Anda "
"mencari tenaga Hamiltonian Ising dua qubit menggunakan primitif Estimator "
"dalam Qiskit.\" />\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By now, you've run your first quantum circuit and learned the basics of "
"quantum computing: how quantum states are represented, how gates act on "
"those states, and how quantum features like superposition and entanglement "
"are involved. Now it's time to put all of this into practice and solve your "
"first problem on a quantum computer.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang, Anda dah jalankan litar kuantum pertama dan belajar asas "
"pengkomputeran kuantum: cara keadaan kuantum diwakili, cara get bertindak ke"
" atas keadaan tersebut, dan cara ciri kuantum seperti superposisi dan "
"keterjeratan terlibat. Kini tiba masanya untuk praktikkan semua ini dan "
"selesaikan masalah pertama Anda pada komputer kuantum.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll explore the broader landscape of quantum-suitable problems in a later "
"lesson. For now, we'll focus on a problem in the domain of nature "
"simulation: using a quantum computer as a cleaner, more controllable stand-"
"in for a natural quantum system. In fact, this was the first application "
"Richard Feynman envisioned for quantum computers in the 1980s. As he "
"famously put it: \"Nature isn't classical, dammit, and if you want to make a"
" simulation of nature, you'd better make it quantum mechanical...\"\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita akan terokai landskap masalah yang sesuai untuk kuantum yang lebih luas"
" dalam pelajaran kemudian. Buat masa ini, kita akan fokus pada masalah dalam"
" domain simulasi alam: menggunakan komputer kuantum sebagai pengganti yang "
"lebih bersih dan lebih terkawal untuk sistem kuantum semula jadi. "
"Sebenarnya, ini adalah aplikasi pertama yang dibayangkan oleh Richard "
"Feynman untuk komputer kuantum pada tahun 1980-an. Seperti katanya yang "
"terkenal: \"Alam semula jadi bukan klasik, celaka, dan kalau Anda nak buat "
"simulasi alam semula jadi, lebih baik buat secara mekanik kuantum...\"\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this lesson, we'll follow that principle to simulate the interaction "
"between two spins, which you can think of as tiny magnets. Depending on the "
"sign of their interaction, they might prefer to align and point in the same "
"direction, or anti-align and point in opposite directions. We'll focus on "
"the latter case because it often leads to more interesting &mdash; and more "
"challenging &mdash; behavior. Once we understand this small two-qubit "
"system, we'll show how the same ideas scale up, allowing quantum computers "
"to take advantage of their exponential scaling when simulating large spin "
"systems.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam pelajaran ini, kita akan ikuti prinsip itu untuk mensimulasikan "
"interaksi antara dua spin, yang boleh Anda bayangkan sebagai magnet kecil. "
"Bergantung pada tanda interaksi mereka, mereka mungkin lebih suka sejajar "
"dan menunjuk ke arah yang sama, atau anti-sejajar dan menunjuk ke arah yang "
"bertentangan. Kita akan fokus pada kes kedua kerana ia sering membawa kepada"
" tingkah laku yang lebih menarik &mdash; dan lebih mencabar. Setelah kita "
"faham sistem dua qubit yang kecil ini, kita akan tunjukkan cara idea yang "
"sama boleh diskala, membolehkan komputer kuantum memanfaatkan penskalaan "
"eksponen mereka apabila mensimulasikan sistem spin yang besar.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Two interacting magnets {#two-interacting-magnets}"
msgstr "Dua magnet yang berinteraksi {#two-interacting-magnets}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For this problem, we're going to use two qubits, one for each spin in our "
"model. Each spin can be pointing up (qubit state $|0\\rangle$), down (qubit "
"state $|1\\rangle$), or in a superposition of the two states.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk masalah ini, kita akan gunakan dua qubit, satu untuk setiap spin dalam"
" model kita. Setiap spin boleh menunjuk ke atas (keadaan qubit "
"$|0\\rangle$), ke bawah (keadaan qubit $|1\\rangle$), atau dalam superposisi"
" dua keadaan tersebut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the spins have an *antiferromagnetic* interaction, it means they want to "
"anti-align, so when one is up, the other wants to be down, and vice-versa.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika spin mempunyai interaksi *antiferomagnet*, ia bermakna mereka mahu "
"anti-sejajar, jadi apabila satu ke atas, yang satu lagi mahu ke bawah, dan "
"sebaliknya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now suppose there is also a magnetic field pointing from left to right in "
"our system. Because this field points across the usual up-down direction of "
"the spins, it is called a transverse field. This field can flip spins, which"
" causes the lowest energy configuration to be a specific superposition of "
"up-and-down spin arrangements rather than any single definite spin "
"pattern.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang andaikan ada juga medan magnet yang menunjuk dari kiri ke kanan "
"dalam sistem kita. Kerana medan ini menunjuk melintasi arah biasa atas-bawah"
" spin, ia dipanggil medan melintang. Medan ini boleh membalikkan spin, yang "
"menyebabkan konfigurasi tenaga terendah menjadi superposisi tertentu susunan"
" spin atas-bawah dan bukannya sebarang corak spin tunggal yang pasti.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can describe all of these effects using a mathematical object called a "
"Hamiltonian. The Hamiltonian tells us the energy of the system for a given "
"arrangement of spins:\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita boleh terangkan semua kesan ini menggunakan objek matematik yang "
"dipanggil Hamiltonian. Hamiltonian memberitahu kita tenaga sistem untuk "
"susunan spin tertentu:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H = J Z_1 Z_0 + h_x (X_1 + X_0)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H = J Z_1 Z_0 + h_x (X_1 + X_0)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $J$ is a coefficient controlling the strength of the interaction "
"between spins and $h_x$ is a coefficient for the strength of the external "
"magnetic field. $Z_1 Z_0$ rewards or penalizes the spins depending on "
"whether they are aligned or anti-aligned, and $X_0$ and $X_1$ represent the "
"spin-flipping effect of the magnetic field.\n"
msgstr ""
"di mana $J$ adalah pekali yang mengawal kekuatan interaksi antara spin dan "
"$h_x$ adalah pekali untuk kekuatan medan magnet luaran. $Z_1 Z_0$ memberi "
"ganjaran atau penalti kepada spin bergantung pada sama ada mereka sejajar "
"atau anti-sejajar, dan $X_0$ serta $X_1$ mewakili kesan pembalikan spin "
"medan magnet.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In physics, systems tend to settle into the state with the lowest possible "
"energy, called the ground state. Finding this lowest-energy state is a "
"common problem, but it requires optimization techniques that are beyond the "
"scope of this lesson.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam fizik, sistem cenderung menetap dalam keadaan dengan tenaga serendah "
"mungkin, dipanggil keadaan dasar. Mencari keadaan tenaga terendah ini adalah"
" masalah yang biasa, tetapi ia memerlukan teknik pengoptimuman yang di luar "
"skop pelajaran ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Instead, we will ask a simpler question: If we prepare the spins in a "
"particular state, what is the energy of that state?\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebaliknya, kita akan tanya soalan yang lebih mudah: Jika kita sediakan spin"
" dalam keadaan tertentu, apakah tenaga keadaan itu?\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "To answer this, we will:\n"
msgstr "Untuk menjawab ini, kita akan:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare the spins in a state of our choosing\n"
msgstr "Sediakan spin dalam keadaan pilihan kita\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Measure the energy of that state using the Hamiltonian above\n"
msgstr "Ukur tenaga keadaan itu menggunakan Hamiltonian di atas\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is exactly the kind of calculation that appears inside larger quantum "
"algorithms, such as variational algorithms, which you can explore in later "
"courses.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini adalah persis jenis pengiraan yang muncul dalam algoritma kuantum yang "
"lebih besar, seperti algoritma variatif, yang boleh Anda terokai dalam "
"kursus kemudian.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Qiskit implementation {#qiskit-implementation}"
msgstr "Pelaksanaan Qiskit {#qiskit-implementation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Before jumping into writing code, we need a bit of context setting. When we "
"run a quantum circuit, we always end by measuring the qubits. But there are "
"two different kinds of questions we might want to ask about the result of "
"that measurement: Sometimes, we just want to know what the state of the "
"qubit is. Other times, we want to know, given the quantum state, what is the"
" value of a physical quantity, like energy?\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebelum mula menulis kod, kita perlu sedikit konteks. Apabila kita jalankan "
"litar kuantum, kita sentiasa berakhir dengan mengukur qubit. Tetapi terdapat"
" dua jenis soalan berbeza yang mungkin kita ingin tanya tentang hasil ukuran"
" tersebut: Kadangkala, kita hanya ingin tahu apakah keadaan qubit. Kali "
"lain, kita ingin tahu, berdasarkan keadaan kuantum, apakah nilai kuantiti "
"fizikal, seperti tenaga?\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In Qiskit, these two types of questions are handled by two different tools, "
"called primitives.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam Qiskit, dua jenis soalan ini dikendalikan oleh dua alat berbeza, "
"dipanggil primitif.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`Sampler` answers the first kind of question. It runs the circuit many times"
" and tells us how often we measure each possible outcome, like `00`, `01`, "
"`10`, or `11`. The result is a histogram that shows the probability of each "
"measurement outcome.\n"
msgstr ""
"`Sampler` menjawab jenis soalan pertama. Ia jalankan litar berkali-kali dan "
"memberitahu kita berapa kerap kita mengukur setiap kemungkinan hasil, "
"seperti `00`, `01`, `10`, atau `11`. Hasilnya adalah histogram yang "
"menunjukkan kebarangkalian setiap hasil ukuran.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`Estimator` answers the second kind of question. Instead of giving us a "
"histogram, it combines many measurements behind the scenes to compute a "
"single number, such as the energy of the state according to a Hamiltonian we"
" provide.\n"
msgstr ""
"`Estimator` menjawab jenis soalan kedua. Berbanding memberikan kita "
"histogram, ia menggabungkan banyak ukuran di sebalik tabir untuk mengira "
"satu nombor tunggal, seperti tenaga keadaan mengikut Hamiltonian yang kita "
"berikan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To help you understand when and why we would use each of these tools, we'll "
"walk through two complete workflows (called \"Qiskit patterns\") applied to "
"the same two-qubit system.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk membantu Anda memahami bila dan mengapa kita menggunakan setiap alat "
"ini, kita akan lalui dua aliran kerja lengkap (dipanggil \"corak Qiskit\") "
"yang digunakan pada sistem dua qubit yang sama.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Qiskit patterns workflow {#qiskit-patterns-workflow}"
msgstr "Aliran kerja corak Qiskit {#qiskit-patterns-workflow}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Qiskit patterns workflow is a general framework we use to solve quantum "
"problems with Qiskit. It breaks a quantum computing task into four steps:\n"
msgstr ""
"Aliran kerja corak Qiskit adalah rangka kerja am yang kita gunakan untuk "
"menyelesaikan masalah kuantum dengan Qiskit. Ia memecahkan tugas "
"pengkomputeran kuantum kepada empat langkah:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Map the problem to a model that can be represented by quantum circuits\n"
msgstr "Petakan masalah kepada model yang boleh diwakili oleh litar kuantum\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Optimize the circuit to be run on a specific backend\n"
msgstr "Optimumkan litar untuk dijalankan pada Backend tertentu\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Execute the optimized circuit on the selected backend\n"
msgstr "Laksanakan litar yang dioptimumkan pada Backend yang dipilih\n"

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Post-process the raw measurement data\n"
msgstr "Proses lepas data ukuran mentah\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Experiment 1: Use `Sampler` to measure the state {#experiment-1-use-sampler-"
"to-measure-the-state}"
msgstr ""
"Eksperimen 1: Guna `Sampler` untuk mengukur keadaan {#experiment-1-use-"
"sampler-to-measure-the-state}"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Map {#map}"
msgstr "Petakan {#map}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In general, the mapping step is where we figure out how to represent a real-"
"world problem in terms of qubits, operators, and measurements. In many "
"applications, this is the trickiest and most involved part of the workflow "
"&mdash; even simple questions, like \"what does each qubit represent?\" do "
"not always have straightforward answers.\n"
msgstr ""
"Secara umum, langkah pemetaan adalah tempat kita fikirkan cara mewakili "
"masalah dunia sebenar dalam bentuk qubit, operator, dan ukuran. Dalam banyak"
" aplikasi, ini adalah bahagian aliran kerja yang paling rumit dan paling "
"melibatkan &mdash; malah soalan mudah, seperti \"apakah yang diwakili oleh "
"setiap qubit?\" tidak selalu mempunyai jawapan yang mudah.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this experiment, however, the mapping is deliberately simple. Each "
"physical degree of freedom maps directly onto a single qubit. Because of "
"this one-to-one correspondence, the mapping step reduces to choosing the "
"quantum state we want to prepare and writing a circuit that prepares and "
"measures that state.\n"
msgstr ""
"Namun dalam eksperimen ini, pemetaan sengaja dibuat mudah. Setiap darjah "
"kebebasan fizikal dipetakan terus ke satu qubit. Kerana perkadaran satu-ke-"
"satu ini, langkah pemetaan menjadi memilih keadaan kuantum yang ingin kita "
"sediakan dan menulis litar yang menyediakan dan mengukur keadaan tersebut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here, we'll prepare an entangled Bell state, similar to the one we made in "
"the very first lesson of this course:\n"
msgstr ""
"Di sini, kita akan sediakan Bell state yang terbelit, serupa dengan yang "
"kita buat dalam pelajaran pertama kursus ini:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\Psi\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(\\vert 10\\rangle - \\vert 01\\rangle)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\Psi\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(\\vert 10\\rangle - \\vert 01\\rangle)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/use-a-qc-"
"today/your-first-quantum-experiment/extracted-"
"outputs/29ade313-4249-480a-a4f3-b96621fd7894-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/use-a-qc-"
"today/your-first-quantum-experiment/extracted-"
"outputs/29ade313-4249-480a-a4f3-b96621fd7894-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Optimize {#optimize}"
msgstr "Optimumkan {#optimize}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Before we run our circuit on a quantum computer (or a simulator if you have "
"exhausted your free time on real quantum computers for the month), we need "
"to prepare it for execution. This step is called optimization. (Note: this "
"use of the word \"optimization\" can be confusing. In quantum computing, "
"optimization problems refer to a specific class of problems. Here, we're "
"using optimization to describe a required preparation step that every "
"quantum circuit goes through before it can be run efficiently on "
"hardware.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebelum kita jalankan litar pada komputer kuantum (atau simulator jika Anda "
"dah habiskan masa percuma pada komputer kuantum sebenar untuk bulan ini), "
"kita perlu sediakan ia untuk pelaksanaan. Langkah ini dipanggil "
"pengoptimuman. (Nota: penggunaan perkataan \"pengoptimuman\" ini boleh "
"mengelirukan. Dalam pengkomputeran kuantum, masalah pengoptimuman merujuk "
"kepada kelas masalah tertentu. Di sini, kita menggunakan pengoptimuman untuk"
" menggambarkan langkah persediaan yang diperlukan yang dilalui setiap litar "
"kuantum sebelum ia boleh dijalankan dengan cekap pada perkakasan.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "During optimization:\n"
msgstr "Semasa pengoptimuman:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We choose the backend &mdash; either a real quantum computer or a "
"simulator.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita pilih Backend &mdash; sama ada komputer kuantum sebenar atau "
"simulator.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We assign our circuit's qubits to physical qubits on the device.\n"
msgstr "Kita tugaskan qubit litar kita kepada qubit fizikal pada peranti.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We rewrite the circuit using only the gates that the quantum computer can "
"actually perform.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita tulis semula litar menggunakan hanya get yang sebenarnya boleh "
"dilaksanakan oleh komputer kuantum.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Optionally implement error mitigation and suppression techniques to reduce "
"the effects of noise.\n"
msgstr ""
"Secara pilihan laksanakan teknik pengurangan dan penindasan ralat untuk "
"mengurangkan kesan bunyi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In Qiskit, this is handled automatically by the transpiler. Once you pick "
"your backend, the transpiler does all the work to make your circuit ready "
"for execution, so you don't have to manually adjust the gates or qubit "
"assignments. The transpiler also offers different optimization levels, which"
" can help reduce errors if needed. The optimization is done in stages called"
" 'passes'. So this optimization will be handled by the `pass_manager` in the"
" code below. To learn more about errors and error mitigation, see Olivia "
"Lane's [Quantum Computing in Practice](/learning/courses/quantum-computing-"
"in-practice) course.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam Qiskit, ini dikendalikan secara automatik oleh Transpiler. Setelah "
"Anda pilih Backend, Transpiler melakukan semua kerja untuk menjadikan litar "
"Anda bersedia untuk pelaksanaan, jadi Anda tidak perlu laraskan get atau "
"tugasan qubit secara manual. Transpiler juga menawarkan tahap pengoptimuman "
"yang berbeza, yang boleh membantu mengurangkan ralat jika diperlukan. "
"Pengoptimuman dilakukan dalam peringkat yang dipanggil 'laluan'. Jadi "
"pengoptimuman ini akan dikendalikan oleh `pass_manager` dalam kod di bawah. "
"Untuk mengetahui lebih lanjut tentang ralat dan pengurangan ralat, lihat "
"kursus [Quantum Computing in Practice](/learning/courses/quantum-computing-"
"in-practice) oleh Olivia Lanes.\n"

