#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Execute {#execute}"
msgstr "Laksanakan {#execute}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we're ready to execute! We'll load Sampler, then send the job to the "
"backend.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kini kita bersedia untuk laksanakan! Kita akan muatkan Sampler, kemudian "
"hantar kerja ke Backend.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Or, if you're using a simulator, you can uncomment and run this cell "
"instead:\n"
msgstr ""
"Atau, jika Anda menggunakan simulator, Anda boleh uncomment dan jalankan sel"
" ini sebaliknya:\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Post-process {#post-process}"
msgstr "Proses lepas {#post-process}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/use-a-qc-"
"today/your-first-quantum-experiment/extracted-"
"outputs/3edb4a9a-2f9a-4713-8b16-b1294ba0ebf6-1.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/use-a-qc-"
"today/your-first-quantum-experiment/extracted-"
"outputs/3edb4a9a-2f9a-4713-8b16-b1294ba0ebf6-1.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We see that the majority of counts are in either `01` or `10`, meaning that "
"when one qubit was measured to be `0`, the other was `1`, and vice-versa. "
"This is consistent with the Bell state $\\vert \\Psi^- \\rangle$ we "
"prepared.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita lihat bahawa majoriti kiraan ada dalam `01` atau `10`, bermakna apabila"
" satu qubit diukur sebagai `0`, yang satu lagi adalah `1`, dan sebaliknya. "
"Ini konsisten dengan Bell state $\\vert \\Psi^- \\rangle$ yang kita "
"sediakan.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Experiment 2: Use `Estimator` to measure the energy {#experiment-2-use-"
"estimator-to-measure-the-energy}"
msgstr ""
"Eksperimen 2: Guna `Estimator` untuk mengukur tenaga {#experiment-2-use-"
"estimator-to-measure-the-energy}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now that we've seen how to sample a quantum state, let's use Estimator to "
"compute the energy of our Bell state $\\vert \\Psi^- \\rangle = "
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(\\vert 01 \\rangle - \\vert 10 \\rangle)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang setelah kita tahu cara sampler keadaan kuantum, jom gunakan "
"Estimator untuk mengira tenaga Bell state $\\vert \\Psi^- \\rangle = "
"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(\\vert 01 \\rangle - \\vert 10 \\rangle)$ kita.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Map {#map-1}"
msgstr "Petakan {#map-1}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As a reminder, the energy of the system is determined by the interaction "
"between the spins ($J$) and the external magnetic field ($h_x$) as captured "
"by the Hamiltonian:\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebagai peringatan, tenaga sistem ditentukan oleh interaksi antara spin "
"($J$) dan medan magnet luaran ($h_x$) seperti yang ditangkap oleh "
"Hamiltonian:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each term in the Hamiltonian tells us how a certain combination of spins contributes to the energy. In Qiskit, we can represent these terms as Pauli operators, which are just labels for simple actions on qubits:\n"
"- $Z_1 Z_0$ acts with a $Z$ on both qubits.\n"
"- $X_0$ acts with $X$ on qubit 0.\n"
"- $X_1$ acts with $X$ on qubit 1.\n"
msgstr ""
"Setiap sebutan dalam Hamiltonian memberitahu kita bagaimana gabungan spin tertentu menyumbang kepada tenaga. Dalam Qiskit, kita boleh wakili sebutan-sebutan ini sebagai operator Pauli, yang hanyalah label untuk tindakan mudah ke atas qubit:\n"
"- $Z_1 Z_0$ bertindak dengan $Z$ pada kedua-dua qubit.\n"
"- $X_0$ bertindak dengan $X$ pada qubit 0.\n"
"- $X_1$ bertindak dengan $X$ pada qubit 1.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A `SparsePauliOp` in Qiskit is a way to store a list of these Pauli "
"operators along with their numerical coefficients. These Pauli operators are"
" the observables that we want the quantum computer to measure &mdash; the "
"quantities that tell us about the system. Using `Estimator`, we can compute "
"the average value of each observable on our state and combine them according"
" to the coefficients in the Hamiltonian to get the total energy.\n"
msgstr ""
"`SparsePauliOp` dalam Qiskit adalah cara untuk menyimpan senarai operator "
"Pauli ini bersama pekali berangka mereka. Operator Pauli ini adalah boleh "
"ukur yang kita mahu komputer kuantum ukur &mdash; kuantiti yang memberitahu "
"kita tentang sistem. Menggunakan `Estimator`, kita boleh mengira nilai "
"purata setiap boleh ukur pada keadaan kita dan menggabungkannya mengikut "
"pekali dalam Hamiltonian untuk mendapatkan tenaga jumlah.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that we omitted the `qc.measure_all()` line in our code. This is "
"because with `Estimator`, we don't need to specify where to measure in the "
"circuit. We will just tell it which observables we want estimated, and "
"Qiskit takes care of the measurements behind the scenes.\n"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahawa kita abaikan baris `qc.measure_all()` dalam kod kita. Ini "
"kerana dengan `Estimator`, kita tidak perlu nyatakan di mana untuk mengukur "
"dalam litar. Kita hanya perlu beritahu ia boleh ukur mana yang kita mahu "
"dianggarkan, dan Qiskit menguruskan ukuran di sebalik tabir.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Optimize {#optimize-1}"
msgstr "Optimumkan {#optimize-1}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The optimization step proceeds as before, with the addition of making sure "
"our observables are also written in a way that the quantum computer can "
"understand.\n"
msgstr ""
"Langkah pengoptimuman diteruskan seperti sebelumnya, dengan tambahan "
"memastikan boleh ukur kita juga ditulis dengan cara yang boleh difahami oleh"
" komputer kuantum.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/use-a-qc-"
"today/your-first-quantum-experiment/extracted-"
"outputs/09d2920c-65c8-4a3c-bdca-0da78f0ad0c1-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/use-a-qc-"
"today/your-first-quantum-experiment/extracted-"
"outputs/09d2920c-65c8-4a3c-bdca-0da78f0ad0c1-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Execute {#execute-1}"
msgstr "Laksanakan {#execute-1}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the Execute step, we'll load `Estimator`, then send the circuit plus the "
"list of observables that we want it to estimate to the quantum computer.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam langkah Laksana, kita akan muatkan `Estimator`, kemudian hantar litar "
"bersama senarai boleh ukur yang kita mahu dianggarkan ke komputer kuantum.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Post-process {#post-process-1}"
msgstr "Proses lepas {#post-process-1}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, in the post-processing step, we simply print the energy calculated "
"behind the scenes by `Estimator`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Akhirnya, dalam langkah proses lepas, kita hanya cetak tenaga yang dikira di"
" sebalik tabir oleh `Estimator`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This is the energy of our state!\n"
msgstr "Inilah tenaga keadaan kita!\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Conclusion {#conclusion}"
msgstr "Kesimpulan {#conclusion}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this lesson, we learned how to prepare a simple two-qubit quantum state "
"representing two interacting spins. We saw how to use `Sampler` to observe "
"the distribution of measurement outcomes and how to use `Estimator` to "
"calculate the energy of the state according to the Hamiltonian. Along the "
"way, we saw how the Hamiltonian encodes the interactions between spins and "
"the effects of an external field, and how different states can have "
"different energies.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam pelajaran ini, kita belajar cara menyediakan keadaan kuantum dua qubit"
" yang mudah mewakili dua spin yang berinteraksi. Kita lihat cara menggunakan"
" `Sampler` untuk memerhatikan taburan hasil ukuran dan cara menggunakan "
"`Estimator` untuk mengira tenaga keadaan mengikut Hamiltonian. Dalam "
"perjalanan ini, kita lihat bagaimana Hamiltonian mengekodkan interaksi "
"antara spin dan kesan medan luaran, dan bagaimana keadaan yang berbeza boleh"
" mempunyai tenaga yang berbeza.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Extension to many spins {#extension-to-many-spins}"
msgstr "Pelanjutan kepada banyak spin {#extension-to-many-spins}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So far, we have only looked at two spins, which is simple enough to analyze "
"by hand. In real physical systems, such as in a magnet or other complex "
"material, there are often many interacting spins. When the number of spins "
"increases, the Hamiltonian becomes more complex and finding the lowest-"
"energy state becomes much harder. This is where quantum computers can help: "
"by preparing different states and estimating their energies, we can explore "
"low-energy configurations more efficiently than classical computers for "
"large systems.\n"
msgstr ""
"Setakat ini, kita hanya lihat dua spin, yang cukup mudah untuk dianalisis "
"dengan tangan. Dalam sistem fizikal sebenar, seperti dalam magnet atau bahan"
" kompleks lain, selalunya ada banyak spin yang berinteraksi. Apabila "
"bilangan spin meningkat, Hamiltonian menjadi lebih kompleks dan mencari "
"keadaan tenaga terendah menjadi jauh lebih sukar. Di sinilah komputer "
"kuantum boleh membantu: dengan menyediakan keadaan yang berbeza dan "
"menganggarkan tenaga mereka, kita boleh meneroka konfigurasi tenaga rendah "
"dengan lebih cekap berbanding komputer klasik untuk sistem yang besar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A natural extension of this experiment would be to increase the number of "
"qubits to represent more spins and adjust the way the spins are prepared to "
"try to find the lowest-energy state. This approach is the essence of "
"variational methods, which you can learn about in the [Variational Quantum "
"Algorithms](/learning/courses/variational-algorithm-design) course.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pelanjutan semula jadi eksperimen ini adalah meningkatkan bilangan qubit "
"untuk mewakili lebih banyak spin dan melaraskan cara spin disediakan untuk "
"cuba mencari keadaan tenaga terendah. Pendekatan ini adalah intipati kaedah "
"variatif, yang boleh Anda pelajari dalam kursus [Variational Quantum "
"Algorithms](/learning/courses/variational-algorithm-design).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There are also other quantum approaches to studying ground-state energies "
"that go beyond variational techniques. These methods are not covered here, "
"but are introduced in the [Quantum Diagonalization "
"Algorithms](/learning/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms) course if "
"you're interested in learning more.\n"
msgstr ""
"Terdapat juga pendekatan kuantum lain untuk mengkaji tenaga keadaan dasar "
"yang melampaui teknik variatif. Kaedah-kaedah ini tidak diliputi di sini, "
"tetapi diperkenalkan dalam kursus [Quantum Diagonalization "
"Algorithms](/learning/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms) jika Anda "
"berminat untuk mengetahui lebih lanjut.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Learning objective {#learning-objective}"
msgstr "Objektif pembelajaran {#learning-objective}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Go back to the beginning of Experiment 2 and retry it with a different "
"superposition state. Can you find a state with even lower energy than the "
"one we used?\n"
msgstr ""
"Kembali ke permulaan Eksperimen 2 dan cuba semula dengan keadaan superposisi"
" yang berbeza. Bolehkah Anda cari keadaan dengan tenaga yang lebih rendah "
"daripada yang kita gunakan?\n"
